menu "Configuration"

config LPAC_WITH_PCSC
	bool "Include APDU PCSC Backend support"
	default y
	help
	  Compile LPAC with APDU PCSC Backend support.

config LPAC_WITH_AT
	bool "Include APDU AT Backend support"
	default y
	help
	  Compile LPAC with APDU AT Backend support.

config LPAC_WITH_UQMI
	bool "Include APDU uqmi Backend support"
	default y
	help
	  Compile LPAC with APDU uqmi Backend support.

config LPAC_WITH_MBIM
	bool "Include APDU MBIM Backend support"
	default y
	help
	  Compile LPAC with APDU MBIM Backend support.

config LPAC_WITH_QMI
	bool "Include APDU QMI Backend support"
	default y
	help
	  Compile LPAC with APDU QMI Backend support.

config LPAC_INSTALL_GSMA_CI_CERTS
	bool "Download GSMA RSP Root CI certificates and add them to the system CA bundle"
	default y
	select PACKAGE_ca-bundle
	help
	  Downloads the following three GSMA "Root Certificate Issuer for
	  Remote SIM Provisioning" root certificates at build time and
	  merges them into /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt. This allows
	  lpac (and any other tool relying on the system CA bundle, e.g.
	  curl) to validate TLS connections to SM-DP+/SM-DS servers.

	  Source of this certificate list:
	  https://www.gsma.com/solutions-and-impact/technologies/internet-of-things/embedded-sim/gsma-root-certificate-issuer-remote-sim-provisioning/ :

	    - Verizon/M2M31 Root CI (DER, M2M variant):
	      https://www.gsma.com/solutions-and-impact/technologies/internet-of-things/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Verizon_GSMA_M2M31-Root-CI21.crt_.txt

	    - Symantec/RSPv2 Root CI (PEM, Consumer variant):
	      https://www.gsma.com/solutions-and-impact/technologies/internet-of-things/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/Symantec_GSMA_RSPv2-Root-CI1.txt

	    - CI SIG OISTE (PEM, eSIM IoT variant, shipped as a .zip):
	      https://www.gsma.com/solutions-and-impact/technologies/esim/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/CERT_CI_SIG_OISTE.pem_.zip

	  All three are fetched, normalized to PEM (converting the DER
	  file and unpacking the zip as needed) and appended to the CA
	  bundle.
endmenu
